{"type":"text","timestamp":1794309514090,"sessionID":"ses_e3ae3a209ffeV5xuHIel72SCA4","part":{"id":"prt_1c52e04e6001s2YI94G2TfrUX9","sessionID":"ses_e3ae3a209ffeV5xuHIel72SCA4","messageID":"msg_1c52dee6400140nADVzJfaC4f7","type":"text","text":"All 3 tests pass. Here's a summary of the three bugs fixed:\n\n| File | Bug | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| `invoice/money.py` | `int(float(amount) * 100)` — floating-point imprecision made `to_cents(\"19.99\")` return `1998` | Use `Decimal(amount) * 100` for exact conversion |\n| `invoice/tax.py` | `net_cents * rate // 100` — floor division truncated instead of rounding half up (399.8 → 399) | Use `Decimal` with `ROUND_HALF_UP` |\n| `invoice/invoice.py` | Discount was applied to gross total at the end; `net_cents()` and `tax_cents()` ignored it entirely | Discount now applies per line before tax; each line's discount amount rounds half up, then tax is computed on the discounted net |","time":{"start":1794309489894,"end":1794309514090}}}
